[h1]R.A.T.S. Flotilla: a test bench for Sea Power[/h1]
[i]R.A.T.S. - Reconnaissance, Acoustics, Terrain & Signals[/i]

Something broke. Was it the game, or one of the 47 mods you swore were fine? Flotilla keeps several Sea Power installs side by side, each with its own mods, settings and saves.

[h2][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3836624723]R.A.T.S. Flotilla[/url][/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Bug reports that count:[/b] one click makes a bone-clean install with no mods and no loader
[*][b]Test a giant mod list[/b] on its own copy. So loaded it's a miracle it starts? Your everyday game never finds out
[*][b]Keep the old version[/b] next to the new one and compare after an update
[*][b]Mods per copy:[/b] on/off, load order, or add a mod to just that copy
[*][b]Name your copies[/b] so you know which one is which
[*]Your Steam install stays exactly as it is
[/list]
A small Windows app, about 19 GB of disk per copy. Also on [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerFlotilla/releases/latest]GitHub[/url].

[i]R.A.T.S. - Ratte's Assorted Tactical Systems[/i]
